.TH DWM 1 dwm\-VERSION
.SH NAME
dwm \- dynamic window manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dwm
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
dwm is a dynamic window manager for X. It manages windows in tiled, monocle
and floating layouts. Either layout can be applied dynamically, optimising the
environment for the application in use and the task performed.
.P
In tiled layouts windows are managed in a master and stacking area. The master
area on the left contains one window by default, and the stacking area on the
right contains all other windows. The number of master area windows can be
adjusted from zero to an arbitrary number. In monocle layout all windows are
maximised to the screen size. In floating layout windows can be resized and
moved freely. Dialog windows are always managed floating, regardless of the
layout applied.
.P
Windows are grouped by tags. Each window can be tagged with one or multiple
tags. Selecting certain tags displays all windows with these tags.
.P
Each screen contains a small status bar which displays all available tags, the
layout, the title of the focused window, and the text read from the root window
name property, if the screen is focused. A floating window is indicated with an
empty square and a maximised floating window is indicated with a filled square
before the windows title.  The selected tags are indicated with a different
color. The tags of the focused window are indicated with a filled square in the
top left corner.  The tags which are applied to one or more windows are
indicated with an empty square in the top left corner.
.P
dwm draws a small border around windows to indicate the focus state.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
prints version information to stderr, then exits.
.SH USAGE
.SS Status bar
.TP
.B X root window name
is read and displayed in the status text area. It can be set with the
.BR xsetroot (1)
command.
.TP
.B Button1
click on a tag label to display all windows with that tag, click on the layout
label toggles between tiled and floating layout.
.TP
.B Button3
click on a tag label adds/removes all windows with that tag to/from the view.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button1
click on a tag label applies that tag to the focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
click on a tag label adds/removes that tag to/from the focused window.
.SS Keyboard commands
.TP
.B Mod4\-x
Spawn
.BR dmenu(1)
for launching other programs.
.TP
.B Mod4\-,
Focus previous screen, if any.
.TP
.B Mod4\-.
Focus next screen, if any.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-,
Send focused window to previous screen, if any.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-.
Send focused window to next screen, if any.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-b
Toggles bar on and off.
.TP
.B Mod4\-c [t/f/m/g]
Sets tiled/floating/monocle/gapless grid layout.
.TP
.B Mod4\-c Shift\-g
Display all window clients in all tags together in a gapless grid layout.
.TP
.B Mod4\-c o
Select view of the window in focus. The list of tags to be displayed is matched to the window tag list.
.TP
.B Mod4\-c Shift\-o
Jump to selected window client from gapless grid layout.
.TP
.B Mod4\-space
Toggles between current and previous layout.
.TP
.B Mod4\-n
Focus next window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-e
Focus previous window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-l
Increase number of windows in master area.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-u
Decrease number of windows in master area.
.TP
.B Mod4\-i
Increase master area size.
.TP
.B Mod4\-h
Decrease master area size.
.TP
.B Mod4\-equal
Restore master area size to default.
.TP
.B Mod4\-bracket[right/left]
View the next/prev tag that has a client window, else view the next/prev tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-bracket[right/left]
View the next/prev tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-[h/i]
Move active client window to next/prev tag and view that tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-[h/i]
Swaps tag on all client windows of selected tag with the next/prev tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-[h/i]
Increase/Decrease tiled client window size.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-o
Restore client window sizes to default within respective stack.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-[n/e]
Swap to next/prev client window from selected client window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-[n/e]
View the prev/next tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-q q
Close focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-q Control\-q
Close all windows in current tag, except focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-q Shift\-q
Close all windows in current tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-q c
Invoke exitmenu for dwm.
.TP
.B Mod4\-q Shift\-c
Restart dwm.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-space
Toggle focused window between tiled and floating state.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-space
Switch focus to tiled master client window from anywhere in the stack.  Return to the client window from the master client by repeating the same keybind.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Tab
Toggles to the previously selected tags.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-[1..n]
Apply nth tag to focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-[1..n]
Add/remove nth tag to/from focused window.
.TP
.B Mod4\-[1..n]
View all windows with nth tag.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-[1..n]
Add/remove all windows with nth tag to/from the view.
.TP
.B Mod4\-[Up/Down/Left/Right]
Move floating windows.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-[Up/Down/Left/Right]
Resize floating windows.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-[Up/Down/Left/Right]
Move floating window to edge of screen.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Control\-Shift\-[Up/Down/Left/Right]
Resize floating window to edge of screen.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Shift\-F5
Reload colors from .Xresources file.
.TP
.B Mod4\-[grave/Shift\-grave/Shift\-equal]
Launch scratchpads for st/emacs capture buffer/st running calc.
.TP
.B Mod4\-a [n/Shift\-n/e/Shift\-e]
Launch scratchpads for st running lf/emacs dired buffer/st running emacs scratch buffer/emacs scratch buffer.
.TP
.B Mod4\-z [n/e/i/o/t/s/r/a]
Jump to first/second/third/fourth/fifth/sixth/seventh/eighth window of current tag.
.SS Mouse commands
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button1
Move focused window while dragging. Tiled windows will be toggled to the floating state.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button2
Toggles focused window between floating and tiled state.
.TP
.B Mod4\-Button3
Resize focused window while dragging. Tiled windows will be toggled to the floating state.
.SH CUSTOMIZATION
dwm is customized by creating a custom config.h and (re)compiling the source
code. This keeps it fast, secure and simple.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dmenu (1),
.BR st (1)
.SH ISSUES
Java applications which use the XToolkit/XAWT backend may draw grey windows
only. The XToolkit/XAWT backend breaks ICCCM-compliance in recent JDK 1.5 and early
JDK 1.6 versions, because it assumes a reparenting window manager. Possible workarounds
are using JDK 1.4 (which doesn't contain the XToolkit/XAWT backend) or setting the
environment variable
.BR AWT_TOOLKIT=MToolkit
(to use the older Motif backend instead) or running
.B xprop -root -f _NET_WM_NAME 32a -set _NET_WM_NAME LG3D
or
.B wmname LG3D
(to pretend that a non-reparenting window manager is running that the
XToolkit/XAWT backend can recognize) or when using OpenJDK setting the environment variable
.BR _JAVA_AWT_WM_NONREPARENTING=1 .
.SH BUGS
Send all bug reports with a patch to hackers@suckless.org.
